WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.825 --> 00:00:12.145
Many districts have a Portrait of a Graduate, or their own social and emotional learning standards. In this video you'll record yours, so we can show how Fixer Nation lessons connect to it.

2
00:00:12.646 --> 00:00:25.356
Before you start, read the note at the top of the page. The connections shown here are Fixer Nation's own suggested matches. They don't mean your district, your state, or CASEL has endorsed our program.

3
00:00:25.857 --> 00:00:39.647
Select Add a framework. Give it a name, and choose a type: a Portrait of a Graduate, or social and emotional learning standards. Then choose your state, and check who published it, which starts out as your district's name.

4
00:00:40.148 --> 00:00:51.728
Then paste the link to your district's official page for it, and check the date. Every framework needs both. That's how we confirm it's the real thing. Year adopted and grade span are optional.

5
00:00:52.229 --> 00:01:02.609
The type can't be changed after you save, so pick carefully. You can have up to three frameworks, and each can hold up to sixty standards. Select Save.

6
00:01:03.111 --> 00:01:11.991
Now add the standards. Select Add a standard. Enter its code, if it has one, a short title, and the grade band if it applies.

7
00:01:12.492 --> 00:01:26.602
Then write a short summary, up to six hundred characters, in your own words. Please don't copy long passages from your district's document. A short summary is enough, and the link to your official page covers the rest.

8
00:01:27.104 --> 00:01:33.734
If the standard lines up with a CASEL competency, you can choose it from the list. Then select Save.

9
00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:36.994
Add the rest the same way, one at a time.

10
00:01:39.596 --> 00:01:44.396
You can edit or delete a standard at any time, using the buttons beside it.

11
00:01:44.897 --> 00:01:50.647
In the next video, you'll suggest connections, and send the framework to us for review.
